---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/placeholderpics/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import meandMiko from '../assets/logo/meandmiko.jpg';
import nazimCupcakes from '../assets/logo/nazimCupcakes.jpg';
---

<Layout
	title="About nazimdev.blog"
	description="The story behind nazimdev.blog."
	pubDate={new Date('August 21 2026')}
	heroImage={meandMiko}
>
	<h3 style="color: #d14280;">How it all started</h3>
			<p style="color: white;">
				The creation of this blog can be traced back to Thursday 18th of June 2026- the MCV Develop Awards. 
				I was only able to attend thanks to an incredibly generous LinkedIn post from <i>Diva Agency</i>, 
				who had a space ticket they didn't want to go to waste. Through my LinkedIn network, and speedy timing, I was able to
				respond to the post in time to secure a ticket hours before the event. I had an incredible time meeting so many new people and
				becoming a sponge for the evening- learning how to network, industry advice and the key piece of advice that led to me creating this blog.
			</p>

			<p style="color: white;">
				To land a role in project management, I need experience on top of my degree and the projects I'd been part of during my time at 
				university. So, maybe in my spare time I could create a game? Teaming up with a few friends and making something sounds like a good way
				to get more hands on experience, but there's one big issue- games take too long to make. Plus, it still won't give me the industry
				standard experience I need. I need a way to show employers that I'm prepared for a role.
			</p>

			<p style="color: white;">
				Since deciding to create this blog, I've been talking to industry professionals, asking them all the same question- 
				"What is the most common problem you find in teams as a project manager?". Doing this has created a list of problems and conversation topics
				that I will explore in this blog, preparing me to tackle problems through independant research and disucssion with industry professionals. 
